# Hugo build output — once GitHub Pages is switched to the Actions deploy
# source (.github/workflows/deploy.yml), this stops being committed and
# should be untracked with `git rm -r --cached docs/` in that same change.
# Left tracked for now: Pages currently serves this repo's docs/ directly
# from the branch, and untracking it here would blank the live site before
# the Actions-based deploy is actually wired up on the GitHub side.
# /docs/

# Hugo caches / locks
/resources/
/.hugo_build.lock

# OS cruft
.DS_Store

# Build output. Published by the GitHub Actions workflow, which builds from
# source on every push — so a tracked copy could only ever be redundant, or
# (as it was) silently stale relative to the source that produced it.
docs/
